# Voice Inbox — repository layout

One **Git repository** with **Yarn 4 workspaces** and **Turborepo** orchestration. Apps live in `web/`, `mobile/`, and `telegram-bot/`; future shared code goes in `packages/*`. **Node:** >= 24.

| App | Package name | Path | Role |
|-----|--------------|------|------|
| Web | `voice-inbox-web` | `web/` | Next.js, Prisma, public site / API / admin |
| Mobile | `voice-inbox-app` | `mobile/` | React Native (CLI), Drizzle, offline-first app |
| Telegram bot | `voice-inbox-telegram-bot` | `telegram-bot/` | Optional Grammy admin bot |

**Install and quality gates from the repository root** (uses committed Yarn 4.17.0 in `.yarn/releases/`):

```bash
node .yarn/releases/yarn-4.17.0.cjs install   # or: yarn install (if no parent Yarn project)
yarn lint
yarn type:check
yarn test
yarn ci                  # full check: format:check, lint, type:check, build, test
yarn ci:affected         # same, only changed packages vs origin/main
yarn validate:affected   # lint + type:check + test only (changed packages)
```

App-specific dev servers: `yarn dev:web`, `yarn workspace voice-inbox-app start` (Metro), etc. You can still `cd` into an app and run its scripts.

**Repo root:** `node scripts/release.mjs` — bump mobile/web semver + native build numbers.

## Monorepo notes

- Single `yarn.lock` at root; `nmHoistingLimits: workspaces` keeps `mobile/node_modules` for React Native autolinking.
- `turbo.json` defines `lint`, `type:check`, `test`, `build`, `dev` pipelines.
- Do not copy Prisma (web) and Drizzle (mobile) schemas between apps.

## Data layers

- **Web:** Prisma + Postgres — admin, `AppConfig`, support, blog, Pro keys; **not** mobile note payloads.
- **Mobile:** Drizzle + SQLite (op-sqlite) — records, transcripts, embeddings locally.

## Docs & legal

- Overview: root `README.md`
- Shared packages placeholder: `packages/README.md`
- Legal Markdown: `web/content/` — see `web/content/README.md` and `.cursor/rules/legal-content.mdc`

## Scope of changes

Change only what the task requires.

## Cursor indexing

Use a root `.cursorignore` so `node_modules`, build outputs, and `.env` are not pulled into context. Keep it up to date when adding new generated directories (`web/generated`, `mobile/drizzle`, etc.).
